<h2 id="spaces-resolve-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0BH7">89.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
This chapter discusses resolution of singularities of Noetherian algebraic spaces of dimension $2$. We have already discussed resolution of surfaces for schemes following Lipman <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Lipman">Lipman</a>]</span> in an earlier chapter. See Resolution of Surfaces, Section <a href="/tag/0ADX" data-tag="0ADX">54.1</a>. Most of the results in this chapter are straightforward consequences of the results on schemes. 
</p>
<p>
Unless specifically mentioned otherwise all geometric objects in this chapter will be algebraic spaces. Thus if we say “let $f : X \to Y$ be a modification” then this means that $f$ is a morphism as in Spaces over Fields, Definition <a href="/tag/0AD8" data-tag="0AD8">72.8.1</a>. Similarly for proper morphism, etc, etc. 
</p>
